      "reason": "French uses a comma as its decimal separator. In French prose, 1,000 ms denotes 1 ms rather than the intended 1000 ms. This conflicts with the preserved code CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MILLIS, 1000 and creates a 1000-fold ambiguity in a timeout value. This is numeric meaning, not an optional style change.",
